exports[`help output warden ui --help (and nested subcommands) 1`] = `
"$ warden ui --help
Usage: warden ui [options] [command]

drive a leased simulator / emulator (agents): status, snapshot, find, open,
press, fill, scroll, …

Options:
  -h, --help                   display help for command

Commands:
  status                       device, lease, helper and recording state
  close                        stop this device's helper (the lease stays);
                               --app also quits the app, --release frees the
                               lease
  snapshot                     the screen as @eN lines (bumps the generation)
  find <selector...>           elements matching a selector, with @eN refs
                               (bumps the generation)
  open <target>                launch an app (bundle id) or open a URL; --metro
                               starts the dev client on that Metro; --kind
                               installs that build first
  press <target...>            tap an element or point; an @eN older than 30 s
                               is re-verified first
  tap <target...>              tap an element or point; an @eN older than 30 s
                               is re-verified first
  fill <args...>               replace a text field's content, then read it back
                               (use -- before text starting with -)
  type <text>                  type into whatever has focus
  key <name>                   press a key: Enter Backspace Tab Space Escape
                               Delete Up Down Left Right
  scroll <direction> [amount]  scroll content: scroll down reveals what is
                               below; --until swipes until a selector is on
                               screen
  alert <action>               answer the system alert / sheet on top, or read
                               it
  home                         press the home button
  back                         press back (Android only)
  screen                       the device screen: orientation, appearance,
                               screenshot, video
  gesture                      touch gestures: swipe, longpress, pinch, rotate,
                               raw paths
  wait <args...>               poll (100 ms, --timeout) until an element is
                               visible; also: absent <sel> | text <…> | stable
                               [ms]
  is <args...>                 exit 0 when the element is in that state, 1 when
                               not
  get <args...>                print one property of an element (count = how
                               many match)
  bench                        time snapshot, press, settle, tree and driver
                               open on this device against the speed targets
  record                       turn a warden ui session into an e2e spec: start
                               <name> | note | use <module#fn> | undo | status |
                               cancel | stop. The journal is kept until a
                               successful stop or cancel
  eval <expression>            run JavaScript in the app (Hermes) and print the
                               value
  tree                         the app's React components (testID, label, text,
                               screen) with rects
  logs [args...]               app console: logs [n] | start | stop | mark
                               <label> | clear
  network [n]                  the app's fetch calls recorded by \`logs start\` or
                               the dev session
  reload                       reload the app's JavaScript
  exceptions                   the app's uncaught exceptions
  route                        the route key of the screen the app is on
  devtools                     the dev session's devtools broker: status |
                               resume
  logpoint                     log a value whenever a source line runs, without
                               pausing: add | list | rm | clear | hits
  help [command]               display help for command

$ warden ui status --help
Usage: warden ui status [options]

device, lease, helper and recording state

Options:
  --udid <udid>          device udid (iOS) / serial (Android)
  --serial <serial>      Android serial
  --lease <id>           use the device behind this lease id
  --claim                take over a stale/missing lease, or claim a device when
                         none is held
  --platform <platform>  platform for --claim with no device named: ios
                         (default) | android
  --physical             with --claim and no device named: claim a connected
                         phone, not an emulator
  --profile <slug>       device profile for --claim with no device named
  --runtime <runtime>    runtime for --claim with no device named
  --force                drive the device even while a live warden process (e2e,
                         batch, run) holds your lease on it; your own warden dev
                         device is shared without it
  --timeout <ms>         deadline in milliseconds (default 5000)
  --no-record            don't append this step to a running recording
  --json                 machine-readable output: one JSON document on stdout
  -h, --help             display help for command

$ warden ui close --help
Usage: warden ui close [options]

stop this device's helper (the lease stays); --app also quits the app, --release
