$ warden ui gesture --help
Usage: warden ui gesture [options] [command]

touch gestures: swipe, longpress, pinch, rotate, raw paths

Options:
  -h, --help             display help for command

Commands:
  swipe <args...>        raw swipe: the way the finger moves (swipe up reveals
                         what is below), or x1 y1 x2 y2
  longpress <target...>  press and hold an element or point (default 800 ms)
  pinch <args...>        two-finger pinch around an element, a point or the
                         screen centre: scale > 1 spreads the fingers (zoom in),
                         < 1 closes them
  rotate <args...>       two-finger rotation (device orientation is \`screen
                         rotate\`): positive degrees turn clockwise
  path                   raw touch paths: one --path per finger (max 2), fingers
                         go down and lift together
  help [command]         display help for command

