$ warden ui record --help
Usage: warden ui record [options] [command]

turn a warden ui session into an e2e spec: start <name> | note | use <module#fn>
| undo | status | cancel | stop. The journal is kept until a successful stop or
cancel

Options:
  -h, --help       display help for command

Commands:
  start <name>     start recording; stop writes <suite specsDir>/<name>.e2e.ts
                   (e2e/<name>.e2e.ts without a suite)
  note <text>      mark a user-visible step; the spec gets it as a comment above
                   the next action
  use <module#fn>  run an exported helper on this device and, when it passes,
                   record a call to it (await fn(fixtures)); a failing helper
                   records nothing
  undo [n]         drop the last recorded step(s), notes included
  status           target, step count, the last 5 steps and the lints so far
  cancel           throw the recording away (a spec already written is left)
  stop             write the spec (or helper), merge ids, print lints, then run
                   the spec once on this device; exit 1 keeps the file AND the
                   journal so you can undo, fix and stop again
  help [command]   display help for command

$ warden ui record start --help
Usage: warden ui record start [options] <name>

start recording; stop writes <suite specsDir>/<name>.e2e.ts (e2e/<name>.e2e.ts
without a suite)

Arguments:
  name                     recording name (the spec file name unless --to)

Options:
  --to <spec>              spec file to write
  --helper <module#fn>     write an exported function into a helpers module
                           instead of a spec, e.g. e2e/helpers.ts#signIn
  --prerequisite <text>    what must be true before the helper runs (its doc
                           comment); needs --helper
  --ids <module>           ids module to merge test ids into (export const ids =
                           { … } as const)
  --options <module#name>  shared test.use options to pass (e.g.
                           e2e/helpers/steps#SPEC_OPTIONS); default: detected in
                           the specs dir, \`none\` passes none
  --title <title>          the generated test's title (default: the name)
  --suite <name>           e2e.<name> suite for the default path and the verify
                           run (needed when several exist)
  --overwrite              replace an existing spec file, or an existing helper
                           function (the shared --force is for a busy device)
  --udid <udid>            device udid (iOS) / serial (Android)
  --serial <serial>        Android serial
  --lease <id>             use the device behind this lease id
  --claim                  take over a stale/missing lease, or claim a device
                           when none is held
  --platform <platform>    platform for --claim with no device named: ios
                           (default) | android
  --physical               with --claim and no device named: claim a connected
                           phone, not an emulator
  --profile <slug>         device profile for --claim with no device named
  --runtime <runtime>      runtime for --claim with no device named
  --force                  drive the device even while a live warden process
                           (e2e, batch, run) holds your lease on it; your own
                           warden dev device is shared without it
  --timeout <ms>           deadline in milliseconds (default 5000)
  --no-record              don't append this step to a running recording
  --json                   machine-readable output: one JSON document on stdout
  -h, --help               display help for command

