  --runtime <runtime>    runtime for --claim with no device named
  --force                drive the device even while a live warden process (e2e,
                         batch, run) holds your lease on it; your own warden dev
                         device is shared without it
  --timeout <ms>         deadline in milliseconds (default 5000)
  --no-record            don't append this step to a running recording
  --json                 machine-readable output: one JSON document on stdout
  --metro <url>          Metro URL (default: WARDEN_METRO_URL, state.json, then
                         this owner's leased ports)
  -h, --help             display help for command

$ warden ui devtools --help
Usage: warden ui devtools [options] [command]

the dev session's devtools broker: status | resume

Options:
  -h, --help      display help for command

Commands:
  status          what the broker is doing: attached, yielded, lost
  resume          take the page back after the broker yielded to Chrome DevTools
  help [command]  display help for command

$ warden ui devtools status --help
Usage: warden ui devtools status [options]

what the broker is doing: attached, yielded, lost

Options:
  --udid <udid>          device udid (iOS) / serial (Android)
  --serial <serial>      Android serial
  --lease <id>           use the device behind this lease id
  --claim                take over a stale/missing lease, or claim a device when
                         none is held
  --platform <platform>  platform for --claim with no device named: ios
                         (default) | android
  --physical             with --claim and no device named: claim a connected
                         phone, not an emulator
  --profile <slug>       device profile for --claim with no device named
  --runtime <runtime>    runtime for --claim with no device named
  --force                drive the device even while a live warden process (e2e,
                         batch, run) holds your lease on it; your own warden dev
                         device is shared without it
  --timeout <ms>         deadline in milliseconds (default 5000)
  --no-record            don't append this step to a running recording
  --json                 machine-readable output: one JSON document on stdout
  -h, --help             display help for command

$ warden ui devtools resume --help
Usage: warden ui devtools resume [options]

take the page back after the broker yielded to Chrome DevTools

Options:
  --udid <udid>          device udid (iOS) / serial (Android)
  --serial <serial>      Android serial
  --lease <id>           use the device behind this lease id
  --claim                take over a stale/missing lease, or claim a device when
                         none is held
  --platform <platform>  platform for --claim with no device named: ios
                         (default) | android
  --physical             with --claim and no device named: claim a connected
                         phone, not an emulator
  --profile <slug>       device profile for --claim with no device named
  --runtime <runtime>    runtime for --claim with no device named
  --force                drive the device even while a live warden process (e2e,
                         batch, run) holds your lease on it; your own warden dev
                         device is shared without it
  --timeout <ms>         deadline in milliseconds (default 5000)
  --no-record            don't append this step to a running recording
  --json                 machine-readable output: one JSON document on stdout
  -h, --help             display help for command

$ warden ui logpoint --help
Usage: warden ui logpoint [options] [command]

log a value whenever a source line runs, without pausing: add | list | rm |
clear | hits

Options:
  -h, --help                   display help for command

Commands:
  add <location> <expression>  log <expression> each time <file:line[:col]> runs
                               (needs \`warden dev\` and a Fusebox debugger)
  list                         the logpoints and whether they are armed
  rm <id>                      remove a logpoint
  clear                        remove every logpoint
  hits [id]                    the values logged so far
  help [command]               display help for command

$ warden ui logpoint add --help
Usage: warden ui logpoint add [options] <location> <expression>

log <expression> each time <file:line[:col]> runs (needs \`warden dev\` and a
Fusebox debugger)

Arguments:
  location     src/x.tsx:42 or src/x.tsx:42:7 (path suffix inside the bundle,
               1-based)
  expression   JavaScript evaluated in the scope of that line

Options:
  --id <id>    name for it (default lp1, lp2, ...)
  --hits <n>   remove it after n hits
  --udid <id>  which dev session (default: the only one)
  --json       print one JSON document
  -h, --help   display help for command

$ warden ui logpoint list --help
Usage: warden ui logpoint list [options]

the logpoints and whether they are armed

Options:
  --udid <id>  which dev session (default: the only one)
  --json       print one JSON document
  -h, --help   display help for command

$ warden ui logpoint rm --help
Usage: warden ui logpoint rm [options] <id>

remove a logpoint

Arguments:
  id           logpoint id

Options:
  --udid <id>  which dev session (default: the only one)
  --json       print one JSON document
  -h, --help   display help for command

$ warden ui logpoint clear --help
Usage: warden ui logpoint clear [options]

remove every logpoint

Options:
  --udid <id>  which dev session (default: the only one)
  --json       print one JSON document
  -h, --help   display help for command

$ warden ui logpoint hits --help
Usage: warden ui logpoint hits [options] [id]

the values logged so far

Arguments:
  id              only this logpoint

Options:
  --since <when>  30s | 5m | 2h | ISO time
  --limit <n>     at most the last n hits (default 50)
  --udid <id>     which dev session (default: the only one)
  --json          print one JSON document
  -h, --help      display help for command"
`;

